### Page 10 of 19

```text
LOTUS Engineering & Sustainability
1
Cover Letter
Dear City of Cheyenne,
Lotus Engineering & Sustainability, LLC (Lotus), in partnership with Wyoming Outdoor Council (WOC), is pleased to submit our response to the RFP for the Cheyenne MSA
Comprehensive Climate Action Plan (CCAP). All contractual responsibility shall rest solely with Lotus, which is not a subsidiary or affiliate with limited resources.
Lotus is a certified women-owned, data-driven, and client-centered sustainability consulting firm located in Denver, Colorado. We have supported dozens of local governments with
their sustainability and equity initiatives, including Climate Pollution Reduction Grant (CPRG) projects. We help our clients develop climate action plans that not only direct the
community toward a more sustainable and vibrant future but also engage community leaders, staff, and the community’s network of stakeholders.
WOC is Wyoming’s oldest independent statewide conservation organization. Our mission is to protect Wyoming’s environment and quality of life now and for future generations. Our
team comprises experts working in climate action and policy who engage in community-led initiatives. As a Wyoming organization, we understand the State’s context and its
policies, politics, and state-specific (public and private) funding mechanisms to reduce emissions and improve air and water quality. Our team is working to support the Northern
Arapaho Tribe as they work to implement their CPRG grant and is working closely with other communities, local governments, and state agencies to apply for and implement
programs through the Inflation Reduction Act. Our greatest strength is forming connections across stakeholder groups, communities, and all levels of governance while supporting
well-informed decision-making.
A high-level overview of the consultant team’s qualifications include:
Over the last five years, Lotus has conducted greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions inventories and developed and implemented similar comprehensive climate action plans for
 dozens of communities across the United States, including the Denver Regional Council of Governments (CPRG), Albuquerque, NM (CPRG), the City of Commerce City (CO), Cit
y and County of Denver (CO), City of Colorado Springs (CO), Larimer County (CO), Chaffee County (CO), Town of Erie (CO), Clear Creek County (CO), City of Bozeman (MT), and the
City of Mission (KS).
WOC understands how to work and engage in Wyoming communities. WOC works to enhance coordination and collaboration across aspects of Wyoming communities and
 Tribal Governments, especially where programs intersect with other federal funding opportunities such as the recently awarded Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) Solar fo
r All grant and Northern Arapaho CPRG grant.
Lotus has helped clients in rural, mountain communities set GHG emission reduction targets and model the GHG emission reduction potential of various sustainability strategies.
We also estimate costs and time commitments for programs and policies.
Both Lotus and WOC have experience planning, developing, and facilitating equitable, multilingual community engagement events to support equitable community-wide
climate action planning processes.
Most importantly, our passion for the work will be clear in all interactions and deliverables. We will ensure existing efforts, partnerships, and ideas, as well as community and
regional best practices, are brought together to create a CCAP that is relevant, actionable, data-centric, science-based, and connected to existing efforts in the community. We
would be honored to support the Cheyenne MSA to create a future that is just, sustainable, and resilient for current and future residents.
Hillary Dobos, President and Owner
Lotus Engineering & Sustainability
